      <div type="clause" n="39">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 39</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXVI. Gif hwa on cierlisces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.8"/> monnes flette gefeohte, mid syx scill. gebete ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.2"/> ceorle.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.9"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXVI. Gif hwa on ciorlisces monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.5"/> flette gefeohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.6"/>, gebete mid VI scll' ðam ciorle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="72" ed="#liebermann"/>Be cyrlisces monnes flettegefeohte. Gyf hwá on ceorlisces mannes flette gefeohte, mid VI scill' gebete ðam ceorle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="73" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in ceorlisces mannes flette<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.10"/> gefeohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.11"/> (id est in rusticani hominis domus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_39.lnote.oe.12"/> area pugnet), quinque sol. emendet ipsi rustico.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="80" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be cyrlisces monnes flettegefeohte.] Gif hwa on cierlisces monnes flette gefeohte, mid syx scill. gebete ðam ceorle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="40" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="338" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXXVI} Gif hwa cierlisces monnes flette gefeohte, mid syx scill gebete ðam ceorle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="73" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_39.lnote.de.1"/> jemand im Hause<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_39.lnote.de.2"/> eines gemeinfreien Mannes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_39.lnote.de.3"/> ficht, büsse er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_39.lnote.de.4"/> dem Gemeinfreien mit 6 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone fights in the house of a common freeman, let him pay the common freeman 6 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="81" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone fights in the house of a commoner, he shall pay the commoner 6 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_39.attnote.n.1"/> compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="415" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone fights in the house of a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>, he is to pay six shillings compensation to the ceorl.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="339" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone fights in a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>’s house, let him recompense the <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> with six shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="274"><label>ramification of</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6">Ine 6–6.4</ref> <quote>four of five Alfredian uses of 'gefeohtan' are scattered ramifications of Ine's law on fighting before the privileged</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="279"><label>same penalty, extended</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6-3">Ine 6.3</ref> <quote>His penalty of six shillings for fighting on a ceorl's 'floor' was the same as Ine's, but this is one of several laws that went on to fix bigger sums</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>cf. (wergeld enumerations)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_70">Ine 70</ref> <quote>Alfred enumerated the wergelds ... five times as against Ine's once (n. 80)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="339"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Hl_11">Hl 11–13</ref> <quote>Compare rulings against fighting in public in Hloþhere and Eadric §7 to §9 [L11–13] and Ine §6.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="339"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6">Ine 6</ref> <quote>Compare rulings against fighting in public in Hloþhere and Eadric §7 to §9 [L11–13] and Ine §6.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><ref target="clause:Af_42-4">Af 42.4</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyr. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyr. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rl <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rl Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Or;</hi> flet <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Or; flet the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-fehte <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-fehte Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. d. <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. d. Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gemeinfreier 8; Schutz 15a. Das Einschiebsel in Inst. wiederholt Inst. II 59a (aus Af 15)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gemeinfreier 8; Schutz 15a. The interpolation in Inst. repeats Inst. II 59a (from Af 15)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Fletz, Diele’ Q, Schmid, gemäss ursprüngl. Sinne. Doch bedeutet das Wort auch das ganze Haus, steht also mit <hi rend="italic">gebures huse</hi> Ine 6, 3 synonym; so nimmt Hn 81, 3 den Satz</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Floor, hall’ Q, Schmid, in accordance with the original sense. But the word also means the whole house, and is thus synonymous with <hi rend="italic">gebures huse</hi> Ine 6, 3; this is how Hn 81, 3 takes the sentence</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘gemeinfrei geboren’ Inst.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘born a common freeman’ Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_39.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ausser <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> (für Getroffenen) <hi rend="italic">and wite</hi> für den Richter. — Q’s Abweichung in der Zahl scheint blosses Verlesen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">besides <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> (for the man struck) <hi rend="italic">and wite</hi> for the judge. — Q’s divergence in the number seems a mere misreading</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_39.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Ine, cap. 6 § 3. In Kent the fine for a similar offence was 6 shillings, but the Kentish shilling contained 20 sceattas; cf. Abt. cap. 15, and the note to Abt. cap. 16.</seg></note>
      </div>
